    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWith ui2 enabled, when the messages pager is focused, we can't edit a file with `:e` or open a buffer (like with `:bN`). New buffers are added which can be confirmed with `:ls` but we need to exit the pager to open any buffer. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`repro.lua`\n```lua\nrequire(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable {}\n```\n\n```bash\nnvim --clean -u repro.lua\n```\n\n1. `:echo` some text and focus the pager\n2. Try editing files `:e foo.txt` (buffer won't open in a window, messages pager remains focused)\n3. `:ls` to check buffers. `foo.txt` is present\n4. `:b foo` (buffer still won't open in a window)\n5. `q` (exit from pager)\n6. `:b` and `:e` works\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWhen ui2 messages pager is focused (`g<`), user should be able to open windows for editing files `:e` and opening buffers `:b`.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1755+geddadd7ab3\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim doesn't have a pager like messages ui\n\n### Operating system/version\n\narchlinux 7.2.7-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.49.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nInstalled nightly version using bob",
